{"id":"356da4c9a74ebb48","group":"58","path":"58/batch13/58-cor-fodor.md","title":"Fodor's Corollary","display":"cor-fodor — Fodor's Corollary","type":"corollary","metadata":{"type":"corollary","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-cor-fodor","aliases":["58-cor-fodor"],"display":"cor-fodor — Fodor's Corollary","depends_on":["[[../batch20/58-thm-fodor.md]]","[[../batch19/58-df-stationary.md]]","[[../batch12/58-df-regressive-function.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"corollary"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-cor-fodor"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-cor-fodor</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"cor-fodor — Fodor's Corollary"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"e3b01159c2b5601b\" href=\"?note=e3b01159c2b5601b\" title=\"../batch20/58-thm-fodor.md\">../batch20/58-thm-fodor.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"b802c3dd76418d95\" href=\"?note=b802c3dd76418d95\" title=\"../batch19/58-df-stationary.md\">../batch19/58-df-stationary.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"aa5065a1f0bd9a7f\" href=\"?note=aa5065a1f0bd9a7f\" title=\"../batch12/58-df-regressive-function.md\">../batch12/58-df-regressive-function.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\kappa,S,f\\in V\">\\(\\kappa,S,f\\in V\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\omega&lt;\\kappa\">\\(\\omega&lt;\\kappa\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Stationary}(S,\\kappa)\">\\(\\mathrm{Stationary}(S,\\kappa)\\)</span> (stationary-subset predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"b802c3dd76418d95\" href=\"?note=b802c3dd76418d95\" title=\"../batch19/58-df-stationary.md\">../batch19/58-df-stationary.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Regressive}_S(f,S)\">\\(\\mathrm{Regressive}_S(f,S)\\)</span> (regressive-function predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"aa5065a1f0bd9a7f\" href=\"?note=aa5065a1f0bd9a7f\" title=\"../batch12/58-df-regressive-function.md\">../batch12/58-df-regressive-function.md</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{cor\\text{-}fodor} \\vdash \\forall\\kappa,S,f\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\\omega&lt;\\kappa\\land\\mathrm{Stationary}(S,\\kappa)\\land\\mathrm{Regressive}_S(f,S)\\to\\exists\\gamma\\in\\kappa\\;\\mathrm{Stationary}(\\{\\alpha\\in S:f(\\alpha)=\\gamma\\},\\kappa)\\Bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{cor\\text{-}fodor} \\vdash \\forall\\kappa,S,f\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\\omega&lt;\\kappa\\land\\mathrm{Stationary}(S,\\kappa)\\land\\mathrm{Regressive}_S(f,S)\\to\\exists\\gamma\\in\\kappa\\;\\mathrm{Stationary}(\\{\\alpha\\in S:f(\\alpha)=\\gamma\\},\\kappa)\\Bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The uncountability condition <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\omega&lt;\\kappa\">\\(\\omega&lt;\\kappa\\)</span> is essential; regularity is already part of the upstream stationary-set predicate.</li>\n<li>This is the stationary-fiber conclusion of <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"e3b01159c2b5601b\" href=\"?note=e3b01159c2b5601b\" title=\"../batch20/58-thm-fodor.md\">../batch20/58-thm-fodor.md</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch20/58-thm-fodor.md","status":"resolved","id":"e3b01159c2b5601b","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch20/58-thm-fodor.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch19/58-df-stationary.md","status":"resolved","id":"b802c3dd76418d95","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch19/58-df-stationary.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch12/58-df-regressive-function.md","status":"resolved","id":"aa5065a1f0bd9a7f","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch12/58-df-regressive-function.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch19/58-df-stationary.md","status":"resolved","id":"b802c3dd76418d95","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{Stationary}(S,\\kappa)$ (stationary-subset predicate, see [[../batch19/58-df-stationary.md]])","embed":false},{"target":"../batch12/58-df-regressive-function.md","status":"resolved","id":"aa5065a1f0bd9a7f","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{Regressive}_S(f,S)$ (regressive-function predicate, see [[../batch12/58-df-regressive-function.md]])","embed":false},{"target":"../batch20/58-thm-fodor.md","status":"resolved","id":"e3b01159c2b5601b","anchor":"ref-6","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Remark]","excerpt":"This is the stationary-fiber conclusion of [[../batch20/58-thm-fodor.md]].","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"\\kappa,S,f\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"\\omega<\\kappa","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Stationary}(S,\\kappa)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Regressive}_S(f,S)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{cor\\text{-}fodor} \\vdash \\forall\\kappa,S,f\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\\omega<\\kappa\\land\\mathrm{Stationary}(S,\\kappa)\\land\\mathrm{Regressive}_S(f,S)\\to\\exists\\gamma\\in\\kappa\\;\\mathrm{Stationary}(\\{\\alpha\\in S:f(\\alpha)=\\gamma\\},\\kappa)\\Bigr)","display":true},{"tex":"\\omega<\\kappa","display":false}],"bytes":1075,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-55"